  "worked_solution": "The area of a square with sides of length $a$ is given by \n\n$$\nA={a}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that $a=7\\,ft.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={a}^{2}={7}^{2}=49\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
